## Troubleshooting (Linux): `docker compose watch` lock path error
Observed on a Linux host (prompt showed `alexlee@OMEN`) when running:
```sh
docker compose watch
```

Error:
```text
cannot take exclusive lock for project "full-stack-fastapi-template": open /run/user/1000/snap.docker/full-stack-fastapi-template.pid: no such file or directory
```

Fix options:
1) Create the missing runtime dir (common when Docker is installed via Snap):
```sh
# Note: `snap.docker` here is a directory name, not a command to run.
mkdir -p /run/user/$(id -u)/snap.docker
docker compose watch
```

2) If `/run/user/$(id -u)` doesn’t exist (common in WSL/non-systemd shells), point `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` somewhere you own:
```sh
export XDG_RUNTIME_DIR="$HOME/.xdg-runtime"
mkdir -p "$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR"
docker compose watch
```

3) If you don’t need file watching, use plain compose:
```sh
docker compose up --build
```

